			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-728312">
									

<p>Why does he need to be contained? Is making SCPs containable some great sign of humility that must be adhered to? It's one thing if it reads "THIS SCP IS WAY TOO BADASS TO CONTAIN. THE FOUNDATION BOWS BEFORE HIS ALMIGHTYNESS."</p>
<p>That's not the case here. It makes sense his condition would render him uncontainable. PLUS, I for one really like that he's basically self-contained not only by his condition, but by his loyalty to the foundation.</p>
<p>I honestly like this article a lot as it is, it just needs some work in tone and structure. It's kind of vague, and needs to describe what is understood about his condition more clearly and more detail.</p>

