			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-728396">
									

<p>i love the concept to this article, i just dont like the overall…feel of how it's written. minor tweaking would fix that though.</p>
<p>as far as him being uncontainable, while he's currently confining himself to site 19, i cant see him doing that forever. i cant see anyone just settling for staying in one place for the rest of their life in a situation like that, unable to kill themselves yet alone. something does need to be done somehow to ensure he remains there, loyalty just doesnt cut it when you think the organization you're loyal to is gone forever.</p>
<p>one possible idea that comes to mind is if they attempt to keep him contained by giving him the illusion that there's something going on that he needs to solve, some conspiracy, some hope for being able to reverse the things he's done, or maybe some greater threat that he needs to protect against. something that gives him a goal to work toward, something he desperately needs to do that he can only do at site 19.</p>
<p>he would still be technically "uncontainable" insofar as he could still leave at any time, but that would make the containment objective be to monitor his activities and come up with ways to keep him occupied, preferably in ways that do not involve other SCP's.</p>
<p>i dont know if that would destroy the tone of helplessness in his situation though, which is one of the strong parts of the article. just some thoughts.</p>

