														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-728465">
									

<p>I also have to go with 'dodgy tone but actually quite good concept'. I don't think making him containable would diminish from the SCP. He wouldn't need to be kept in a cell, even, normal accomodation and the run of the facility would be fine if dangerous objects were secured.</p>
<p>I'm not sure having a malevolent entity is a good idea. It might require a lot more work and detail to make it interesting than it would be worth. Personally I would just make it a strange incident of his perception rather than some unknown puppetmaster specifically trying to confuse him for no explained reason, but previous posters seem to think it's ok so never mind I guess.</p>
<p>Since he's a Foundation employee we would have all his background information so a nod to that might be worthwhile, just in the vein of 'see document black squares for SCP-451's personnel file'.</p>

							</div>

								
